Description: manageable and configured self-hosting server
 YunoHost aims to make self-hosting accessible to everyone. It configures
 a Web server alongside a LDAP base (email is an optional app, not part of
 the default install). It also provides facilities to manage users,
 domains, apps and so.
 .
 This package contains the NostrHost server-management engine, renamed from
 the historical `yunohost` binary package (Stage 2 of the core rename). It
 Provides/Replaces/Conflicts the old name so existing installs upgrade
 cleanly; a transitional empty `yunohost` package depends on it. The CLI
 and API entry points live in the python3-nostrhost package (the native
 replacement for the retired moulinette framework).

Package: python3-nostrhost
Architecture: all
Section: python
Depends: python3-all (>= 3.11), nostrhost-core
 , python3-typer, python3-bottle, python3-requests
 , python3-nostrhost-auth
Description: native nostrhost framework — moulinette replacement
 nostrhost is the native framework layer that replaces the retired
 moulinette in the YunoHost fork: interface primitives (core, i18n, ui,
 logging, locking, auth) plus the native Typer command-line tool
 (/usr/bin/nostrhost) and the Bottle+NIP-98 HTTP API (/usr/bin/nostr-api).
 .
 It depends on nostrhost-core (its CLI/API import yunohost.nostr_operations
 and friends), while nostrhost-core depends back on it for the framework
 primitives — a legal circular dependency resolved by apt.

Package: yunohost
Architecture: all
Section: utils
Depends: nostrhost-core (>= 12.1.41.19)
Description: transitional package (core renamed to nostrhost-core)
 Empty dependency package so existing installs and scripts that reference
 `yunohost` keep resolving after the engine moved to nostrhost-core. This
 package installs nothing itself. It can be removed once nothing depends on
 the `yunohost` name.
